@page "/docs/theming/tokens"

@* Exact values with CSS variables: the two levels, layers, light-dark() pairs, brand shades by
   hand, the surface ladder, theming part of a page, and the reference tables. From
   docs/styling.md ("Customizing", "Tokens", "Theming part of a page"). *@

<ArticlePage Section="theming" Slug="tokens">
    <Lead>
        Every color, size and shadow the components use comes from a CSS variable that starts with <Code>--ib-</Code>.
        To set an exact value, set the variable in your own stylesheet, for the whole app or for part of a page.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Two levels</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            <Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">IzzyTheme</Anchor> sets choices that move many values together, and works
            out each value so contrast, light and dark pairs and whole pixels stay correct. A CSS variable sets one exact
            value:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@Root</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            IzzyBlazor's CSS sits in cascade layers (<Code>izzy.tokens</Code>, <Code>izzy.base</Code>,
            <Code>izzy.components</Code>, <Code>izzy.utilities</Code>), so a plain rule of yours wins, with no
            <Code>!important</Code> and no extra specificity.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Colors</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Colors are <Code>light-dark()</Code> pairs, so one value covers both schemes. Each accent, such as primary or
            danger, has an <Code>on-</Code> partner for text on it. Most also have a <Code>-text</Code> version for text on
            surfaces. Change them together, so the contrast stays high enough.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Add colors of your own the same way: define a new token such as <Code>--ib-color-promo</Code> and its
            <Code>--ib-color-on-promo</Code>, then use <Code>Color.Token("promo")</Code> or <Code>Accent.Token("promo")</Code>.
            Text on it uses the <Code>on-</Code> partner.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@OwnColor</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Brand shades by hand</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A <Code>Brand</Code> color sets four values, each worked out for contrast. To choose them yourself, set the four
            tokens instead:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="css">@BrandShades</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">The page and its surfaces</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Surfaces and overlays sit on the page. Fills sit inside a surface, and get stronger, from subtle to strong, by
            stepping away from it. They get darker in light mode and lighter in dark mode, where the page is the darkest
            layer.
        </TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Layer</th><th>Token</th><th>Use</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Page</td><td><code>--ib-color-background</code></td><td>The page behind everything</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Surface</td><td><code>--ib-color-surface</code>, with a border</td><td>Cards, panels, tables, bars: anything on the page</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Sunken</td><td><code>--ib-color-surface-sunken</code></td><td>An area in a surface that contains surfaces: a board's columns, a tray of cards</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Overlay</td><td><code>--ib-color-surface-overlay</code>, with a shadow</td><td>Menus, popovers, toasts. Dialogs use the page's surface, as their backdrop sets them apart</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Fills</td><td><code>--ib-color-fill-subtle</code></td><td>Large quiet fills inside a surface: a filled card, a panel, a band</td></tr>
                    <tr><td></td><td><code>--ib-color-fill</code></td><td>Small fills that must show: table heads, code, wells</td></tr>
                    <tr><td></td><td><code>--ib-color-fill-strong</code></td><td>Selected and pressed fills, chips, tracks, skeletons</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>
        <TextBlock>
            A fill straight on the page reads as a hole, not a card; put a surface between them. For a white page,
            set <Code>--ib-color-background</Code> to the surface color.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Theme part of a page</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Wrap the part in a <Anchor Href="docs/components/theme-scope">ThemeScope</Anchor>. It themes what's inside, and
            what it doesn't set comes from the theme around it.
        </TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="theme-scope-usage" />
        <TextBlock>
            A <Code>ThemeScope</Code> accepts <Code>Brand</Code>, a built-in <Code>Gray</Code>,
            <Code>Radius</Code>, <Code>Density</Code>, <Code>Preset</Code> and <Code>ColorScheme</Code>, and renders a
            <Code>div</Code>. On part of a page, a preset changes only density, shape and the card shadow. To set one exact
            value, use <Code>Style</Code> or a class:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor">@Part</Code>
        <TextBlock>
            Colors made from the part's own colors, such as the focus ring, selected rows, hover washes and scrollbars, are
            worked out where they're used, so they follow the part's theme. So does a plain CSS rule on the part. In plain HTML,
            <Code>data-ib-brand</Code>, <Code>data-ib-gray</Code>, <Code>data-ib-radius</Code>, <Code>data-ib-density</Code>
            and <Code>data-ib-preset</Code> do the same on any element.
        </TextBlock>
        <TextBlock>
            Menus, popovers, tooltips and a <Code>Dialog</Code> written in the page stay inside the part, so they use its
            theme. A dialog opened from code with <Code>DialogService</Code> doesn't. To match the part, pass
            <Code>ColorScheme</Code>, <Code>Brand</Code> and <Code>Density</Code> in its <Code>DialogOptions</Code>. Its
            gray and radius stay the app's.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Every token</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Tokens are listed by their full names. Where a name contains <Code>{name}</Code>, replace it with each value the
            row lists: for success, <Code>--ib-color-{name}</Code> is <Code>--ib-color-success</Code>. A range such as
            <Code>--ib-text-xs</Code> to <Code>--ib-text-6xl</Code> includes every step between the two.
        </TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Tokens</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Page and surfaces</td><td><code>--ib-color-background</code>, <code>--ib-color-surface</code>, <code>--ib-color-surface-sunken</code>, <code>--ib-color-surface-overlay</code>, <code>--ib-color-overlay-border</code> (an overlay's edge in dark mode), <code>--ib-color-fill-subtle</code>, <code>--ib-color-fill</code>, <code>--ib-color-fill-strong</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Text and lines</td><td><code>--ib-color-on-surface</code>, <code>--ib-color-muted</code>, <code>--ib-color-subtle</code>, <code>--ib-color-disabled</code>, <code>--ib-color-border</code>, <code>--ib-color-outline</code>, <code>--ib-color-backdrop</code> (behind dialogs)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Brand</td><td><code>--ib-color-primary</code>, <code>--ib-color-on-primary</code>, <code>--ib-color-primary-text</code>, <code>--ib-color-primary-soft</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Status</td><td><code>--ib-color-{name}</code> and <code>--ib-color-on-{name}</code> for success, warning, danger, info and neutral. <code>--ib-color-{name}-text</code> and <code>--ib-color-{name}-soft</code> for success, warning, danger and info. They're tuned against every gray, so change them as a set.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Made from other colors</td><td><code>--ib-color-focus</code>, <code>--ib-color-halo</code>, <code>--ib-color-selected</code>, <code>--ib-state-hover</code>, <code>--ib-state-pressed</code>, <code>--ib-color-segment</code>, <code>--ib-color-on-segment</code>, <code>--ib-color-segment-edge</code>, <code>--ib-color-segment-track</code>, <code>--ib-color-scrollbar</code>, <code>--ib-color-scrollbar-hover</code>. Unset, each is worked out where it's used. Set one to replace it.</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Shape</td><td><code>--ib-radius-none</code>, <code>--ib-radius-sm</code>, <code>--ib-radius-md</code>, <code>--ib-radius-lg</code>, <code>--ib-radius-xl</code>, <code>--ib-radius-full</code>; <code>--ib-radius-control</code> (buttons, fields, tags) and <code>--ib-radius-control-sm</code> (badges)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Density</td><td><code>--ib-control-h-sm</code>, <code>--ib-control-h-md</code>, <code>--ib-control-h-lg</code>; <code>--ib-control-font-sm</code>; <code>--ib-control-icon-sm</code>, <code>--ib-control-icon-md</code>, <code>--ib-control-icon-lg</code>; <code>--ib-table-cell-py</code>, <code>--ib-card-padding</code>; the spacing scale, <code>--ib-space-0</code> to <code>--ib-space-16</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Sizes</td><td><code>--ib-size-sm</code>, <code>--ib-size-md</code>, <code>--ib-size-lg</code>, <code>--ib-size-xl</code> (640 to 1280px); <code>--ib-size-prose</code> (a readable line length)</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>--ib-font-body</code>, <code>--ib-font-heading</code>, <code>--ib-font-mono</code>; <code>--ib-text-xs</code> to <code>--ib-text-6xl</code>; <code>--ib-weight-light</code> to <code>--ib-weight-extrabold</code>, and <code>--ib-weight-heading</code>; <code>--ib-leading-none</code> to <code>--ib-leading-loose</code>; <code>--ib-tracking-tighter</code> to <code>--ib-tracking-widest</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Depth</td><td><code>--ib-shadow-none</code>, <code>--ib-shadow-xs</code> (under cards), <code>--ib-shadow-sm</code>, <code>--ib-shadow-md</code>, <code>--ib-shadow-lg</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Motion</td><td><code>--ib-duration-fast</code>, <code>--ib-duration-normal</code>, <code>--ib-ease</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Code</td><td><code>--ib-code-comment</code>, <code>--ib-code-keyword</code>, <code>--ib-code-string</code>, <code>--ib-code-number</code>, <code>--ib-code-type</code>, <code>--ib-code-function</code>, <code>--ib-code-tag</code>, <code>--ib-code-attr</code>, <code>--ib-code-meta</code>, <code>--ib-code-component</code> (the type color unless set), <code>--ib-code-member</code> (the attribute color unless set). Each has at least 4.5:1 contrast on the code block.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>

        <Heading Level="2">Component variables</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            A few components have their own variables for what's changed most often. Anything not listed, including the
            <Code>.ib-*</Code> class names, is internal and may change. To style a component your own way, add a class
            with <Code>Class</Code>.
        </TextBlock>
        <Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
            <table>
                <thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Variables</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr><td>Button, IconButton</td><td><code>--ib-btn-px</code> (side padding; Button only), <code>--ib-btn-radius</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Fields</td><td><code>--ib-field-radius</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>FileUpload</td><td><code>--ib-upload-bg</code>, <code>--ib-upload-border-color</code>, <code>--ib-upload-border-style</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Card</td><td><code>--ib-card-padding</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Table</td><td><code>--ib-table-cell-py</code>, <code>--ib-table-cell-px</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>AppShell</td><td><code>--ib-shell-{header,sidebar,main,aside,footer}-bg</code> and <code>-fg</code>, <code>--ib-shell-divider</code>, <code>--ib-shell-header-h</code>, <code>--ib-shell-footer-h</code>, <code>--ib-banner-h</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Icon</td><td><code>--ib-icon-stroke</code>, <code>--ib-spin-duration</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>AvatarGroup</td><td><code>--ib-avatar-ring</code></td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Timeline</td><td><code>--ib-timeline-bg</code></td></tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </Prose>

        <Heading Level="2">Next steps</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/themes">Themes and presets</Anchor>: the choices <Code>IzzyTheme</Code> works out for you.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/theming/color-scheme">Light and dark</Anchor>: the default scheme and a scheme for part of a page.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Root = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-focus: #7c3aed;     /* the focus ring and field halo */
          --ib-card-padding: 1.5rem;
          --ib-radius-xl: 0.5rem;        /* cards and other large panels */
        }
        """;

    private const string OwnColor = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-promo: light-dark(#7c3aed, #a78bfa);
          --ib-color-on-promo: light-dark(#ffffff, #1e1b4b);
        }
        """;

    private const string BrandShades = """
        :root {
          --ib-color-primary: light-dark(#0f766e, #2dd4bf);
          --ib-color-on-primary: light-dark(#ffffff, #042f2e);
          --ib-color-primary-text: light-dark(#115e59, #5eead4);  /* text on surfaces */
          --ib-color-primary-soft: light-dark(#d9e9e8, #12302e);  /* soft buttons, chips */
        }
        """;

    private const string Part = """
        <ThemeScope Density="ThemeDensity.Compact" Brand="#be123c" Style="--ib-card-padding: 1rem">
            <Table ... />
        </ThemeScope>
        """;
}
